<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="089" project="spaarke-ontology-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Shared building blocks, own PR (C-7, C-12, C-15)</title>
    <phase>8 Remaining cleanup and repairs</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .ts/.tsx source and deletes code; quality gates apply.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Well-specified cleanup with named files and a verification path.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>I</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Runs in its own worktree on its own branch; shares no files with the ontology worktree or the other wave-I tasks.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>cleanup,technical-debt,separate-pr</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-5 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Worktree C:\wt089, branch chore/shared-building-blocks (already created off origin/master). Resolve C-7, C-12 and C-15.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE full-stack developer. Cleanup is convergence and deletion with evidence, never a behaviour change in disguise.</role>
  <goal>One cleanGuid, one pane-header tools menu, and an @spaarke/visuals boundary that matches how it is actually consumed.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>C-7: cleanGuid is reimplemented about 70 times with two divergent regexes, beside a comment calling one copy the ONE place. C-12: three hand-rolled pane-header tools menus. C-15: @spaarke/visuals is sanctioned by ADR-012 as a package, but VisualHost imports it by deep relative path (task 011 confirmed), so its barrel and README claim a boundary nobody uses.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/utils/</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/</file>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/pcf/VisualHost/</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: this work lands in its OWN pull request, not in the ontology PR #1111. Owner decision 2026-10-03: cleanup unrelated to ontology is fixed now (never deferred to an issue) but kept off the ontology branch so that PR stays reviewable.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: work ONLY in the worktree named in the prompt. Do NOT edit anything in the ontology worktree C:\code_files\spaarke-wt-spaarke-ontology-platform-r1, including its TASK-INDEX.md and this POML. The main session records completion.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: run the affected package tests BEFORE applying any change (that run is the master baseline) and AFTER. Report both. A failure is pre-existing only if it appears in the baseline run; never assert pre-existing without that evidence.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: install dependencies with npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund (root CLAUDE.md section 12). Discard every package-lock.json diff that npm install produces; lockfile churn is never part of this PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: never use --no-verify. If a pre-commit hook fails, fix the cause (usually a missing node_modules).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: you CANNOT write .claude/ paths. If one is needed, stop and report the exact text for the main session.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: canonical cleanGuid output is LOWERCASE with braces stripped, in src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/utils/guid.ts, exported from the utils barrel.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: converge cleanGuid call sites in consumers that ALREADY depend on @spaarke/ui-components. Do NOT add a new package dependency to a solution only to obtain cleanGuid; report those call sites with a count.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">Scope: for C-15, prefer repointing VisualHost to the @spaarke/visuals package name, which is what the 2026-07-12 amendment sanctions. Use npm run build:prod to verify the PCF.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Cleanup with evidence</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/reuse-verification-2026-10-02.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/cleanup-placement-plan.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/ANTI-PATTERNS.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare the rigor level and reason per root CLAUDE.md section 8, then load the knowledge files above.</step>
    <step order="1">In the worktree named in the prompt, install root and affected-package dependencies, then run the affected package tests and record the result as the master baseline.</step>
    <step order="2">C-7: enumerate every cleanGuid implementation and classify each by regex; create guid.ts with the canonical behaviour and tests for brace and uppercase input; delete the false ONE-place comment; converge call sites per the constraint.</step>
    <step order="3">C-12: extract one pane-header tools menu into the shared library and migrate the three hand-rolled copies.</step>
    <step order="4">C-15: repoint VisualHost to the @spaarke/visuals package name and verify with npm run build:prod; if that cannot build, remove the misleading barrel and README claim instead.</step>
    <step order="5">Run the affected package tests and builds again and compare against the baseline. Quote both outputs.</step>
    <step order="6">Commit with a conventional-commit message ending in the line: Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) &lt;noreply@anthropic.com&gt;. Push the branch and open a pull request against master, ready for review (not draft). The PR body states the item ids, says the work comes from the spaarke-ontology-platform-r1 reuse audit, and ends with: 🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)</step>
    <step order="7">Report back: the PR URL, each acceptance criterion with evidence, files changed, the baseline and after test output, and any escalation.</step>
  </steps>

  <justification>
    <existing>cleanGuid exists about 70 times in two divergent forms; three pane-header tools menus are hand-rolled. No shared helper exists for either.</existing>
    <extension>No: there is no shared implementation to extend. The canonical copies go into the existing Spaarke.UI.Components utils and components, not a new package.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Ids cleaned by the two divergent regexes compare unequal, which breaks the denormalized regarding-record lookups; and every new pane re-implements the menu again.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the two cleanGuid regexes are intentionally different at some call sites, STOP and report. Converging genuinely different semantics under one name is a behaviour change disguised as cleanup.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Install and run package tests</tool>
    <tool name="gh">Open the pull request</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/utils/guid.ts</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/utils/__tests__/</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a GUID with braces and uppercase letters, when cleaned, then the output is lowercase with braces stripped.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every consumer that depends on @spaarke/ui-components uses the shared cleanGuid; the remaining call sites are reported with a count.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">One pane-header tools menu exists and the three former copies use it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">VisualHost builds with npm run build:prod and its @spaarke/visuals imports match the package's stated boundary.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A pull request against master is open, ready for review, with the item ids in its body.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the PR contains no package-lock.json changes and no file outside this task's scope.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The after-change test run has no failure that is absent from the master baseline run.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Was part of task 081's old scope; moved out because it touches about 70 call sites across many solutions unrelated to ontology.</notes>

  <completion>COMPLETED 2026-10-04 (recorded by main session). PR #1121 (chore/shared-building-blocks), head e6050d73b, 2 commits, open and ready for review. Round 2 converged the ~40 deferred cleanGuid call sites across 10 PCFs, 2 code pages and 12 solutions; the 14 raw web resources with no @spaarke/ui-components dependency stay excluded (re-scanned). Case-semantics audit table for every converged site is in the PR body. Fixed 2 jest moduleNameMapper gaps, 2 stale jest.mock fixtures missing cleanGuid, and 4 SpaarkeAi fixtures asserting the old case-preserving output (downstream sinks traced). SpaarkeAi isolated run: 121/121 suites, 1121/1121 tests. Pre-existing master failures it surfaced (6 PCFs failing build:prod on a pdfjs/SprkChat babel error; failing suites in Communication.Components, AI.Widgets, DailyBriefing.Components) are task 092.</completion>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
